## Recovery review

`run -> _recover_projection -> recovery_reducer -> repository.recover_projection -> _adopt_completed_projection` remains unchanged (`runtime.py:1275–1324`, `production_runtime.py:1359–1377`, `artifacts.py:3765–3789`). A current-round checkpoint supplies its exact records and generation, after which `runtime.py:2976–2978` returns `_completed_result` before role or rendering work. `_completed_result` has no direct critic requirement (`runtime.py:1647–1667`) and invokes existing cleanup only.

Cleanup reuses prior completed cleanup or recovers exactly owned leases, checks cleanup result counts, and uses its existing dedicated timeout (`runtime.py:1587–1645`). This does not refresh new-work time. Without a current-round checkpoint, scheduling recovery preserves the prior record projection and paid-role/journal recovery, while `_recover_projection` retains its new-work deadline gate. Create-only record publication authenticates identical existing bytes through the unchanged `_create_only_with_status`; no replacement policy was added.

`CandidateArchiveReducerV5.apply` at `search.py:772–805` advances `next_round_index` and records each hypothesis novelty key for every record, independently of archive admission. `_scheduling_history` at `production_runtime.py:1439–1482` consumes checkpoint-owned records, preserves stopping at unfinished/runtime-failed rounds, and rejects record/terminal conflicts. Thus rejected-only history is retained without an archive candidate.

Historical actual06 remains on `runtime.py:2981–3002`'s existing terminal return path. The live branch change does not reopen that outcome. No changes to publication, recovery, adoption, cleanup, reducers or saved deadline handling were necessary for the B4b rejection forms.

